ntury pomp, Walter Bagehot described the City of London as =E2=80=9Cby far =
the greatest combination of economical power and economical delicacy that t=
he world has ever seen=E2=80=9D. In the 20th century, James Madison=E2=80=
=99s famous =E2=80=9Cten miles square=E2=80=9D of Washington DC surely beca=
me the locus of the world=E2=80=99s power and prestige. And today? Today it=
 is in the cluster of low-slung warehouses and digital otherworlds known as=
 Silicon Valley that our fates are most obviously decided.&nbsp;</span>
</p><p style=3D"margin:0;font-size:18px;mso-line-height-alt:21px">&nbsp;</p=
><p style=3D"margin:0;font-size:18px;mso-line-height-alt:27px">
Last weekend, the news was dominated by the scandal of Nvidia chief Jensen =
Huang=E2=80=99s downfall, which rattled markets and diplomats alike. This w=
eekend it is the stock market flotation of Anthropic, a company founded jus=
t five years ago. Anthropic=E2=80=99s valuation reached an astonishing $2tr=
n but has now fallen back again to a mere $1.2trn, as the debate over just =
how valuable AI really is continues to ebb and flow.&nbsp;</p><p style=3D"m=
argin:0;font-size:18px;mso-line-height-alt:21px">&nbsp;</p><p=20
style=3D"margin:0;font-size:18px;mso-line-height-alt:27px">
<span style=3D"word-break: break-word; font-size: 18px;">This debate centre=
s on Claude, the Anthropic chatbot whose abilities are the bedrock of the c=
ompany=E2=80=99s value. Our Silicon Valley correspondent Danny Fortson <a h=
ref=3D"https://link.thetimes.com/click/48551461.449362/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cudGhl=
